I have a complete picture. Here are my findings.

## Summary

The per-city hard limit of 50 owners **exists and is enforced**, but `capacityWarning` **does not yet exist in production code** — it is only referenced by a test that expects it. It appears to be a feature that needs to be implemented, modeled on the existing `bulkSignupWarning` pattern.

---

### 1. Owner capacity per city — the hard rejection at 50

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/OwnerRegistrar.java`** (lines 211-217):

```java
String cityKey = IdentityUtils.normalizeIdentity(owner.getCity());
long ownersInCity = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
    .filter(existing -> IdentityUtils.normalizeIdentity(existing.getCity()).equals(cityKey))
    .count();
if (ownersInCity >= 50) {
    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);   // 409 hard rejection
}
```

Note: the count is done in-memory by streaming `findAllOwners()` and filtering on a normalized city key — there is **no** dedicated repository count-by-city method (see #4).

### 2. Where `capacityWarning` is / should be set

`capacityWarning` is **not defined anywhere in production code** — no field, no DTO property, no mapping. The only reference is the test (see #5). The parallel existing feature is `bulkSignupWarning`, which shows exactly where a `capacityWarning` would need to be wired:

- **Owner model field**: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` line 87 (`private Boolean bulkSignupWarning;` with getter/setter at lines 213-218). A `capacityWarning` field would be added here.
- **Set on create**: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/OwnerRegistrar.java` line 221: `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(ownersCreatedThatDay > 80);` — a `setCapacityWarning(...)` call would go near here, right after the capacity block at lines 211-217 (the `ownersInCity` count is already computed there and could drive the 40-49 warning).
- **OpenAPI DTO schema**: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2324-2332 define `bulkSignupWarning` as a `readOnly` boolean. `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec (there is no hand-written `OwnerDto.java`), so a `capacityWarning` property must be added here to appear in the response.
- **Mapper**: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — `toOwnerDto(Owner)` at line 59. `bulkSignupWarning` maps implicitly by name (no explicit `@Mapping`), so a matching `capacityWarning` field on both `Owner` and `OwnerDto` would map automatically.

### 3. Service class handling owner creation/registration

- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/OwnerRegistrar.java`** — a `@Component` (line 50-51) that holds all the create/registration business logic. Entry point `register(OwnerFieldsDto, ...)` at lines 116 and 131; persists via `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` at line 231.
